            project, due the following Monday, October 12th.
        </p>

        <p>
            An oil slick spreads at sea.
            From time to time, but irregularly, a helicopter is dispatched to
            photograph the oil slick.
            On each trip, the helicopter arrives over the slick, the pilot takes
            a picture, waits 10 minutes, takes another, and heads home.
            On each of seven trips the size (in area) of the slick is measured
            from both photographs.
            The data is given in the table below for the size of the oil slick
            in square miles:
        </p>

        <tabular top="minor" bottom="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
            <col width="30%" halign="center"/>
            <col width="70%" halign="center"/>
            <row header="yes">
                <cell>Initial Observation</cell>
                <cell>10 min. later</cell>
            </row>

            <row>
                <cell>1.047</cell>
                <cell>1.139</cell>
            </row>

            <row>
                <cell>2.005</cell>
                <cell>2.087</cell>
            </row>

            <row>
                <cell>3.348</cell>
                <cell>3.413</cell>
            </row>

            <row>
                <cell>5.719</cell>
                <cell>5.765</cell>
            </row>

            <row>
                <cell>7.273</cell>
                <cell>7.304</cell>
            </row>

            <row>
                <cell>8.410</cell>
                <cell>8.426</cell>
            </row>

            <row>
                <cell>9.117</cell>
                <cell>9.127</cell>
            </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
            The data is coded in the cell below for you to use for the following
            questions.
        </p>

        <program language="python">
